# Normalize line endings to LF for every text file, regardless of contributor
# OS. A Windows checkout (core.autocrlf) would otherwise get CRLF, which breaks
# bash scripts (a stray `\r` under `set -euo pipefail`), the justfiles, and
# `just fmt-check`. CI runs on Linux and expects LF.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Shell scripts must always be LF (explicit; also covered by the rule above).
*.sh text eol=lf

# Binary assets: never normalize line endings or treat as text.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
